        <p>William Crossley, aged forty-three, was executed at Manchester on To-sia y, for the murder of his landlady, Marc Ann Allen,of Lomss-St7,l3urnley, on the 11th June, lw striking her several blows on the head with an axe RUPTURES. TRUSSES. WOODEND'3 PATENT ths most comfortable truss ever invented. A boon to wearers, hiring no spring at back. Single Is. d 3 Double 12s. Carriaue pßid. Send size in inches tc J Woousxn. Chemist. 22. Pitt-street, Liverpo3l.—Advt.</p>
        <p>Mr. Fay, an American millionaire, claims that he is the only man in ,the world who inhabits a mansion built in the air. His house whith is situated in Guana- juator, is over three hundred feet high, and is supported by massive iron pillars. Cricket is not the only game at which Dr.. W. G. Grace excels, He is a capital billiard player, a first- cla-s she, and can hold his own with most men at a hand of whist.</p>
